{"step_index":186,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T07:40:02Z","input_tokens":2103,"cache_read_tokens":99589,"output_tokens":2400,"content":"Here is the complete audit of your entire computer, showing **where every gigabyte is stored**, **what is already backed up**, and **what remains**.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Full PC Disk Breakdown\n\n- **Total SSD Size:** 512 GB (Internal NVMe SSD)\n- **Used Space:** **144 GB**\n- **Free Space:** 324 GB\n\n| Location | Size | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`/home/melwinabi`** | **111 GB** | Your user home directory (see detailed breakdown below) |\n| **`/usr` + `/opt`** | **23 GB** | Ubuntu OS binaries, system libraries, and Linux software installations |\n| **`/var` + `/boot` + `/etc`** | **10 GB** | Linux kernel, boot files, system logs, and snap daemon images |\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 1. What is ALREADY Backed Up to GitHub ([`Ubuntu_Backup`](https://github.com/melwinabi/Ubuntu_Backup))\n\nAll your source code, project files, and personal documents are safely pushed:\n- **`srm/`**: Complete SRM project, architecture diagrams, and flowcharts.\n- **`Documents/`**: All active codebases (`Finance_Folio`, `Smart_Hub`, `Smart_Switch`, `PPV projects`, `NBR_ACEW`, `PlatformIO`, `KiCad_Project`, notes).\n- **`StudioProjects/`**: Android Studio project (**`chat_bot_financial_trading`**).\n- **`STM32CubeIDE/`**: STM32 workspace projects (**`workspace_2.1.1`**).\n- **`Arduino/`**: Custom sketches (**`test_sensor`**, **`test_assi_senro`**, and libraries).\n- **`Downloads/`**: All documents, PDFs, resumes, and project downloads.\n- **`Pictures/`**: All photos and screenshots.\n- **`configs/` & `system_info/`**: `.bashrc`, `.gitconfig`, and complete lists of installed APT packages and Snaps.\n- **`drawing.svg`**: Vector graphic file.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ 2. What REMAINS on the PC (Not on GitHub)\n\nThe remaining **~105 GB** in your home directory falls into these 3 categories:\n\n#### Category A: Large Files Excluded from GitHub (> 90 MB Limit)\n*These could not be uploaded to GitHub due to file size limits:*\n1. **`ACER_Windows.zip` (2.3 GB)** & **`ACER_Windows` (3.0 GB)**: Old files from your previous Acer Windows machine.\n2. **`Documents/OneDrive` (4.1 GB)**: D\n<truncated 251 bytes>\n4` (184 MB)**: Video file.\n5. **Linux Installers in Downloads**: `android-studio-linux.tar.gz` (1.4 GB), `st-stm32cubeide.zip` (805 MB), and `.deb` packages (VS Code, Discord). *Note: Linux installers cannot run on Windows anyway.*\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you need `anime_anniversary_video_created.mp4` or `ACER_Windows.zip`, upload them to **Google Drive** or **OneDrive** before installing Windows. The software installers (`kicad.exe`, `KEIL`, etc.) can simply be downloaded fresh on Windows.\n\n---\n\n#### Category B: Caches & Trash (Safe to Delete / Ignore)\n*These take up the majority of your disk space and do NOT need to be backed up:*\n- **Ubuntu Trash (`.local/share/Trash`): 27 GB** — Deleted files currently sitting in your Ubuntu recycle bin.\n- **Linux Toolchains & Dependencies (~20 GB):**\n  - `.arduino15` (7.2 GB): ESP32/STM32 board cores downloaded by Arduino IDE (Arduino IDE on Windows will download these fresh).\n  - `.gemini` (7.4 GB): AI tool caches.\n  - `.cache` (4.9 GB): System and browser temporary cache.\n  - `Android/Sdk` (4.2 GB): Linux Android SDK files (Android Studio on Windows installs the Windows SDK).\n  - `.gradle`, `.npm`, `.platformio` (~6.8 GB): Package manager caches.\n\n---\n\n#### Category C: Browser Data & Bookmarks\n- **Google Chrome Profile (`.config/google-chrome` - 5.5 GB):**\n  - **Action Required:** Open Chrome and ensure **Sync is turned ON** for your Google account. This automatically backs up your bookmarks, passwords, and extensions to the cloud so they reappear when you install Chrome on Windows.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Final Pre-Install Checklist\n\n- [x] All code repositories, projects, and documents pushed to GitHub (`melwinabi/Ubuntu_Backup`